# Experimental/diagnostic ZDLs staged in dist/ for convenient Effect Manager
# upload. dist/ is what the install docs tell people to point Effect Manager at,
# so these must never be committed -- a stray diagnostic ends up on a stranger's
# pedal. build_all.py's stray-probe guard only knows about plugins registered in
# DIAGNOSTIC_PLUGINS, and these are not, so it cannot catch them. A `git add -A`
# would otherwise sweep them straight in.
# NAM captures (dist/NAMLite-<name>.ZDL) also embed a user's private capture
# weights, so they must never be committed either.
dist/NAM*
dist/CabIR.*

# Archived NAM trial builds. They embed a user's private capture weights, so they
# must never be committed (the loader templates in tools/nam_template/ are
# capture-free; these are not).
build/nam-archive/
# HYBRID IR test bank: inherited Zoom runtime + a user-supplied commercial IR (not redistributable)
dist/IRMesa*
build/ir-archive/
# CabIR cab files: fits of user-owned IRs, not redistributable
dist/C[0-9][0-9]*
# Built from a private capture (amptrec weights)
build/capture-art/*.ZDL
# local test-host build artifact
build/tonic-validation/host.so
# Redraw probe (test A, docs/pedal-research/animated-covers.md): staged for upload, never shipped
dist/Redraw.ZDL
dist/Redraw.png
# CoverRW probe (test C): staged for upload, never shipped
dist/CoverRW.ZDL
dist/CoverRW.png
# Blink probe (test D): staged for upload, never shipped
dist/Blink.ZDL
dist/Blink.png
# Zoom's and TI's files: kept locally, never published (docs/STOCK-FILES.md).
# Zoom firmware and what was extracted from it
firmware/*
!firmware/wrap_for_dis6x.py
# Zoom's stock effects (the effect database and analysis tools read them)
stock_zdls/
# Code extracted from stock effects; the linker needs these locally
build/linesel_handlers.bin
build/air_knob3_edit.bin
build/divf_rts.bin
build/exciter_outlv_edit.bin
build/lofidly_handlers.bin
build/syncprobe_handler*.bin
build/syncprobe_v2_handler.bin
build/TI_section_flags.bin
build/c6xabi_attributes.bin
